  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-memory-vi",
      "text": "Per-project long-term memory for DeepSeek Harness (DSH), backed by SQLite.\n\nThe plugin registers three tools: `memory_save`, `memory_recall`, `memory_search`.\nMemories are scoped per project (derived from the session working directory), so\neach project keeps its own long-term context across sessions.\n\n- No native dependencies: uses `node:sqlite` (Node 22.19+ / 24+).\n- Data lives in `$DSH_HOME/memory/memory.db` (default `~/.dsh/memory/memory.db`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add \"github:zxck5xz/dsh-memory-vi#main\"\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web` (or the desktop app) after adding."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Ask the model to remember things in a session, e.g.:\n\n- \"Lưu lại rằng dự án này dùng port 3000\" → `memory_save`\n- \"Nhớ lại kiến trúc của dự án này\" → `memory_search` / `memory_recall`"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `memory_save` | Save a memory: `content` (required), `key` (optional), `tags` (optional). |\n| `memory_recall` | Retrieve one memory by `key`. |\n| `memory_search` | Keyword search across `content`/`key`, optional `tags` filter, `limit` (default 10). |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "```yaml"
    },
    {
      "section": "profile cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "- id: dsh-memory-vi\n  name: dsh-memory-vi\n  config:\n    root: C:/data/memory   # optional; defaults to $DSH_HOME/memory\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run build   # tsc -> lib/\nnpm test        # runs db selfcheck\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
